  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "The challenge of recognizing people today, especially in the hybrid world, is finding meaningful things to recognize them for. The limitation to our typical approach to praise is that we can only recognize what we see, observe, or learn about from others and our recognition focuses on what we appreciate, which is not always what others want to be appreciated for.\n\n[This article](<HBR_A_Better_Way_to_Recognize_Your_Employees>) shares a new technique: reflective recognition, an inquiry-based approach where an individual or group is invited to reflect on and share what they are proud of and why.",
